{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":1044,"name":"Dr Davide Castiglione","username":"Casti","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.igelsociety.org/casti/{size}/430_2.png","created_at":"2024-10-17T11:26:39.528Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi all, I am writing to you because I need advice regarding a poetry questionnaire that you can find here: \u003ca href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1hy_2V-hP8M2elHVJDn2tgJBkdCCPFm6hmpc196G7fLk/viewform?edit_requested=true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eImagery questionnaire (google.com)\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs I am now collecting responses, it dawned on me that I don’t know if there is a formula to estimate sample size for questionnaires. I have found some papers online (including the one you recommend in another thread of Concordance) but they are very technical and I don’t know if they apply to my case. So basically this is my design in a nutshell:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ematerials: a set of 8 poems; each participant reads 2 poems randomly chosen by the program and answers some questions\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003efor each poem a mixture of tasks is required, mostly open questions and Likert scales.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ethe study is exploratory, the stimuli materials were not chosen according to specific hypotheses (e.g., low vs high imagery poems) but rather to represent the variety of the ‘poems’ population.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI am interested in poetry reading in general (so the set of 8 poems) but also on each specific poem (to account for differences in style). So I am interested in an item-analysis, not in participant-analysis. I want to see how responses to each poem compare, not how specific individuals or groups of individuals respond to poems.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor now I have \u003cstrong\u003e73\u003c/strong\u003e responses but I think I need more: so far, each poem has been read, rated and commented by an average of 18 participants. Is it enough? are there any recommended standards?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA related question concerns the recruitment of participants in ways other than word-of-mouth and online postings: I have seen that some studies use either Amazon Mechanical Turk or Crowdflower, but I guess funding is needed in these cases, and I don’t have it, unfortunately. What would you recommend doing?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThank you in advance for your help!\u003cbr\u003e\nDavide\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"updated_at":"2024-10-17T11:26:39.528Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":23,"reads":9,"readers_count":8,"score":116.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":701,"topic_slug":"help-required-with-estimating-sample-size-for-online-poetry-questionnaire","display_username":"Dr Davide Castiglione","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1hy_2V-hP8M2elHVJDn2tgJBkdCCPFm6hmpc196G7fLk/viewform?edit_requested=true","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Imagery questionnaire","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":227,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"event":null,"calendar_details":[],"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"can_vote":false},{"id":1045,"name":"Willie van Peer","username":"Willie","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/w/838e76/{size}.png","created_at":"2024-10-22T09:59:15.567Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi David,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eyes, there are formulae to calculate how many recipients you need, but I am rather ignorant of them. But I would say: just start!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWould not a call for help on the PALA website be of help???\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWillie\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"updated_at":"2024-10-22T09:59:15.567Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":6,"readers_count":5,"score":1.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":701,"topic_slug":"help-required-with-estimating-sample-size-for-online-poetry-questionnaire","display_username":"Willie van Peer","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":65,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"event":null,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false},{"id":1046,"name":"Danil Fokin","username":"Danil_Fokin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discourse.igelsociety.org/danil_fokin/{size}/276_2.png","created_at":"2024-10-26T12:26:00.989Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, Davide.\u003cbr\u003e\nI am using GPower 3.1. to calculate parameters depending on statistics I am going to apply.\u003cbr\u003e\nYou can check it here:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ca href=\"https://www.psychologie.hhu.de/arbeitsgruppen/allgemeine-psychologie-und-arbeitspsychologie/gpower\" class=\"onebox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://www.psychologie.hhu.de/arbeitsgruppen/allgemeine-psychologie-und-arbeitspsychologie/gpower\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI hope I may be helpful in some aspects.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBest wishes,\u003cbr\u003e\nDanil\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"po